                         12-column grid with OFFSET seams — row 1 splits 7/5,
                         row 2 splits 5/7 — so the vertical join moves as the
                         eye travels down. DOM order matches visual order on
                         every breakpoint, including the single-column
                         collapse below 900px. */}
                    {/* HEADING LEVEL. These were `h4` under the `h2`
                         "Projects", skipping h3 entirely (WCAG 1.3.1 / 2.4.10
                         heading order). `.card-title` is a class, so h3 renders
                         byte-identically — and it also matches projects.astro,
                         which already used h3 for the same class.

                         LINK NAME. Each tile is one big `<a>`, so its accessible
                         name was the concatenation of everything inside it:
                         measured 295 / 113 / 141 characters. `aria-labelledby`
                         pointing at the tile's own title makes the name the
                         title; the rest of the tile still reads as content. */}
                    <div class="project-grid">
                        <a class="card project-card project-feature reveal spotlight" aria-labelledby="pc-kaching-title" href="/projects#cs-finance-title">
